WEBVTT

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:12.570
<b>I tried coming alone to our usual park.</b>

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.070
<b>It's a feeling I've never felt.</b>

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:21.660
<b>Like a child, frightened by the sound of the wind</b>

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.670
<b>I ran back along the path home.</b>

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:33.970
<b>The sky outside the window is too vast. Where are you now?</b>

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.130
<b>Please, may this reach you...</b>

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:44.690
<b>Dear Lord, if you ever grant wishes,</b>

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:50.110
<b>grant my wish right now, please!</b>

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:56.240
<b>I want to hear your voice, I miss you! I want to see you now!</b>

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:00.830
<b>Why must you already be looking toward tomorrow?</b>

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:06.210
<b>Don't just brush it off, saying the time has slipped by.</b>

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.540
<b>Once more...</b>

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:14.550
<b>I love you, and yet it's been too late since long ago.</b>

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:19.140
<b>Even if I give up, it can't be like the past.</b>

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:24.350
<b>Don't just decide so simply there's no way, no choice.</b>

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:28.230
<b>Smile once more.</b>

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.010
It was a totally breeze...

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:48.100
Was it?

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:03.950
Whoa, hold it there.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:06.350
If you wanna get through here you're
gonna have to show us what you got.

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:09.390
You got somethin' to say to that, huh?

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:21.970
What's with you?

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:23.340
You all scared?

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:24.540
Then I'll...

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:25.520
Don't!

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:27.250
That guy's...

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:29.890
...dangerous.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:07.960
So Joey, what's Holly been doing since then?

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:10.910
She's totally got a crush on Heroman.

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:13.040
Heroman!

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:14.600
My hero!

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:16.590
I hope I can meet him again soon!

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:17.300
...like that.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.940
It's really annoying every day.

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:23.300
Guess it won't be good for her to 
learn more than she already does.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:24.090
Yeah...

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:28.890
Well, at least being able to worry about this 
stuff is proof that peaceful days are back.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:31.980
But someone, even now...

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:35.580
...is trying to wreck havoc on that peace!

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:37.390
Professor?

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:38.850
Did something happen?

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:43.300
I think I should tell you 
the details after school.

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:46.770
After class is over, meet up in my lab.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.780
Those three...

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:53.290
They're plotting something again.

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:03.270
Lina, sure you don't need to go to practice?

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:07.270
Yup! I still have time, so 
don't worry about me. Go on.

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:09.490
I see...

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:12.050
Uh, where should I start?

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:15.190
What? Did you do something bad again?

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:19.230
O-O-Of course not!

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:21.030
I w-would never...

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:21.970
In that case...

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:25.760
You should just talk normally...

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:26.700
Right?

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:29.290
Yes, of course.

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:33.840
Fine, let me begin.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:38.210
It was this morning that I began 
to realize the situation.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:43.900
Last night, a research lab for a
pharmaceutical company was attacked.

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:45.600
A pharmaceutical company?

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:48.790
Why would someone attack a place like that?

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:50.450
And that's not all.

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:52.450
I realized when I started looking into it,

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:57.190
but there have been many facilities that 
have been attacked these past few weeks.

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:01.970
All these places were attacked?

00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:02.860
Yes.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:05.360
The attacks happened at a 
university, a military industrial plant,

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:10.650
a government facility, a 
foodstuffs maker, etc, etc...

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:12.980
They seem completely random, however...

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:45.410
I conjecture they were all 
attacked by the same individual.

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:48.680
How do you know that?

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:51.660
Before I tell you my conclusion, look at this.

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:54.400
What is it?

00:05:54.400 --> 00:06:00.340
These are research labs that have stopped
functioning due to accidents or some other reason.

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:01.840
So, these too?

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:04.400
It's not been revealed to the public,

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:07.850
but I suspect these places have also 
been attacked by the same culprit.

00:06:07.850 --> 00:06:09.050
And?

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:12.890
What's the link between these 
seemingly random labs?

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:15.000
Indeed, exactly that!

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:18.750
These incidents are all linked together.

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:19.560
And that link is...

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:21.310
It's...

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:25.320
The legacy of the Skrugg!

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:30.050
Stop your resistance!

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:31.200
Give yourself up quietly!

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:32.650
If you don't...

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:47.690
Wait!

00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:01.050
The places that were attacked 
may have had different aims,

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:04.900
but they were all researching leftover 
Skrugg weapons and wreckage.

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:07.960
That's what I surmise.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:08.990
I see.

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:10.200
Makes sense to me.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:12.660
So then, who is behind it?

00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:15.280
Well, I haven't yet...

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:18.330
Do you have an idea what the next 
place to be attacked will be?

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:20.400
Well, I haven't yet...

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:23.350
Then, what do you know?

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:26.340
Nothing in particular.

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:29.320
Oh...

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:32.610
Just telling us to be careful out there?

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:33.630
Oh, no!

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:34.760
I've got to get to practice!

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:38.260
See everyone later!

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:40.680
Sure...

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:42.750
Later...

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:48.390
So, Professor, is that all you wanted to say?

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:49.220
No.

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:54.700
Now I get to the good part.

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:59.700
I didn't want to say it with 
Lina here, but there's more.

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:02.750
I don't want to get her involved, see.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:04.500
You lied?

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:05.970
Some lies are justified.

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:07.650
Look at this.

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:09.960
It's the map from before, right?

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:13.840
If I connect them in the order of attacks...

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:20.300
This is like a map of the culprit's movements.

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:23.350
They are moving from the central 
US toward the west coast.

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:25.470
You're right...

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:28.110
And my guess for their next target is...

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:35.090
Center City.

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:44.320
We'd better start patrolling Center City then.

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:45.210
Yeah.

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:48.100
And shouldn't we tell the old dude at the NIA?

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:49.420
Um, you guys...

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:54.060
It'd be easiest to ask Mr. Hughes to look into 
the places that might be researching the Skrugg.

00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:55.260
Uh, I'm trying to tell you...

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:56.650
Yeah, you're right.

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:58.670
You guys!

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:01.300
Listen!

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:06.410
I actually have a guess to
where they'll be attacking.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:08.310
Where?

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:10.190
Here.

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:12.050
Yup, right here.

00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:21.120
Hey now...

00:09:21.610 --> 00:09:23.910
You kept it?

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:26.020
Yeah, my bad...

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:29.710
So you want us to protect 
the scrap you picked up?

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:32.010
But won't this be good in the end?

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:34.650
With this we can lure out the culprit!

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:37.650
Do you have any proof they'll be coming here?

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:39.930
That's not a problem.

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:42.180
Just think about it.

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:46.690
All the research labs the culprit 
attacked must have been top secret.

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:49.940
But they found out about them!

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:52.380
So you mean...

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:54.940
Exactly!

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:59.950
They must have some special ability 
that lets them discover the locations!

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:03.830
They always attack at night.

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:06.340
We'll go over the specifics until then.

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:07.590
Right!

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:07.590
Got it.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:24.970
The multi-purpose hall?

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:26.720
Why here?

00:10:26.720 --> 00:10:32.000
We won't get the public involved 
no matter what happens here.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:35.590
I sent the school a note that 
we were doing an experiment.

00:10:35.590 --> 00:10:38.600
We don't need to worry 
about the security guards.

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:41.110
But then don't we need to keep a lookout?

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:42.660
Don't worry.

00:10:43.390 --> 00:10:47.160
I've installed security sensors at 
various locations around the school.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:51.170
If the culprit breaks in, we should 
get a signal on this terminal.

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:54.830
So all that's left is to wait?

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:56.690
That's right.

00:11:07.550 --> 00:11:09.180
Oh, gimme that!

00:11:13.510 --> 00:11:15.770
Hurry up and play, Professor.

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:24.120
It's here!

00:11:25.050 --> 00:11:25.910
What is it?

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:27.290
Calm down!

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:27.910
Calm down!

00:11:28.270 --> 00:11:29.800
First, everyone calm down.

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:32.620
Take your own advice, damn it.

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:34.500
So, what'll we do?

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:35.930
Well...

00:11:37.310 --> 00:11:38.300
I'll go!

00:11:39.560 --> 00:11:41.930
I'd rather not damage the school...

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:44.150
I'll contact you if anything happens.

00:11:44.150 --> 00:11:45.360
Got it.

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:46.720
Don't do anything crazy.

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:48.430
Right.

00:12:12.590 --> 00:12:17.040
Heroman... Engage!

00:12:41.230 --> 00:12:42.230
It's up here...

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:44.950
Round the corner and then...

00:12:54.470 --> 00:12:57.670
We'll capture them, and drag them out at once!

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:06.500
You're...

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:20.440
Joey?

00:13:22.270 --> 00:13:24.200
Ms. Collins?

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:27.260
What are you doing here, Joey?

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:30.300
And look at that toy on your arm.

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:32.670
What?

00:13:32.670 --> 00:13:37.060
I mean... So <i>you're</i> the culprit, Ms. Collins?

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:38.340
Culprit?

00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:39.750
What are you talking about?

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:42.800
Uh, about the Skrugg...

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:48.510
I figured you guys were up to something 
and came to stop you, that's what.

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:53.280
You three are always doing strange 
experiments or sneaking around outside...

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:54.960
It's gone far enough!

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:58.450
You're always causing problems.

00:13:58.450 --> 00:14:02.160
I tell you to stop, but you 
refuse to listen.... Why?

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:05.340
Professor Denton's an adult, too...

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:07.440
He really needs to stop doing 
these sorts of things.

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:09.830
Are you listening, Joey?

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:10.910
Uh, right!

00:14:11.190 --> 00:14:12.290
What?

00:14:12.290 --> 00:14:13.690
Are you hiding something?

00:14:13.690 --> 00:14:16.400
No, nothing at all!

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:18.250
What are you talking about?

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:21.680
There's nothing there.

00:14:24.350 --> 00:14:25.950
Well, of course!

00:14:25.950 --> 00:14:27.510
You're weird, Joey.

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:38.090
What was that sound?

00:14:38.090 --> 00:14:39.670
The experiment!

00:14:39.670 --> 00:14:44.060
He wanted to show the nature of the relationship
between subliminal stimuli and the hall!

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:47.070
It seems like the experiment is dangerous 
though, so I came to stop him!

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:49.330
I knew it.

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:50.450
Fine, then I will...

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:51.500
No!

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:53.160
It might be dangerous!

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:56.450
That's even more reason 
for me not to let you go!

00:14:56.730 --> 00:15:00.460
No, I mean it might be dangerous for <i>you</i>!

00:15:00.460 --> 00:15:01.980
For me?

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:05.210
Anyway, I'll take responsibility 
and bring the two back with me!

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:08.170
Ms. Collins, wait here!

00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:10.000
Got it?!

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:12.590
I'm going now!

00:15:21.500 --> 00:15:23.850
What a handful they are.

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:30.820
T-There it is!

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:33.700
Hey, who are you?

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:40.450
Hey! Can you hear me?

00:15:42.660 --> 00:15:44.620
I've got a bad feeling about this...

00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:46.180
I knew it.

00:15:46.180 --> 00:15:47.520
A Skrugg?

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:49.250
Professor?

00:15:49.250 --> 00:15:49.920
Right!

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:53.650
Always strike first!

00:15:55.930 --> 00:15:59.960
Take this!

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:07.330
Professor!

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:08.950
Got it!

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:11.610
It's after this!

00:16:12.290 --> 00:16:14.750
Don't give it up, no matter what!

00:16:20.810 --> 00:16:22.090
Professor!

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:52.390
Joey, you're late!

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:55.640
Sorry, I had to deal with stuff.

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:03.350
Heroman...

00:17:04.300 --> 00:17:06.180
Attack!

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:41.740
Heroman!

00:17:48.840 --> 00:17:49.880
Joey!

00:18:11.890 --> 00:18:13.070
That's...

00:18:15.050 --> 00:18:16.310
Will!

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:18.260
Why?

00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:20.570
I thought you regained your humanity...

00:18:23.430 --> 00:18:25.220
Where have you been all this time?

00:18:25.220 --> 00:18:27.120
Everyone was worried about you!

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:28.340
Especially Lina!

00:18:34.950 --> 00:18:36.100
Joey!

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:44.610
Psy!

00:18:48.650 --> 00:18:49.650
Will...

00:18:54.910 --> 00:18:58.740
Why do you hesitate?

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:03.120
I am no longer human!

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:04.030
Stop it!

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:06.160
Will!

00:19:28.180 --> 00:19:29.270
Why?

00:19:29.650 --> 00:19:31.810
Why are you doing this?

00:19:31.810 --> 00:19:34.270
What are you attacking humans for?

00:19:34.820 --> 00:19:37.660
Didn't you return to the old Will?

00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:39.750
What do you know?

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:45.660
You all should keep on 
having fun playing "hero."

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:47.700
Playing hero?

00:19:48.050 --> 00:19:50.610
Sometimes you have to accept the bitter reality.

00:19:50.610 --> 00:19:56.170
Forced to fight even when you 
know what awaits you afterwards.

00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:57.550
That's why...

00:19:58.740 --> 00:20:01.840
I'm fighting to protect what's important to me!

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:07.240
If you are the light, then I am the darkness.

00:20:08.530 --> 00:20:12.500
The inhuman existence that 
crawls through the darkness...

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:17.730
I cannot allow traces of the Skrugg 
to be left on this planet.

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:22.880
So I will destroy them all!

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:24.740
What's the meaning behind it?

00:20:25.150 --> 00:20:28.320
What you see with your eyes is not everything.

00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:32.000
Things have already begun to 
move underneath the surface.

00:20:32.280 --> 00:20:33.510
Now listen.

00:20:33.510 --> 00:20:36.010
The next time you try and get in my way...

00:20:36.010 --> 00:20:38.500
I will not hold back, no matter who you are!

00:20:38.820 --> 00:20:40.750
Remember that well!

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:14.290
I see...

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:17.790
To think that Will was actually behind it all.

00:21:18.150 --> 00:21:19.690
What'll we do now?

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:24.540
If we leave him be, the number 
of victims will only increase.

00:21:24.950 --> 00:21:30.950
Sure, but choosing to fight is 
just too difficult a choice.

00:21:30.950 --> 00:21:35.650
We can't leave him alone, but we 
can't fight against Will either.

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:39.060
This is a hard problem.

00:21:40.260 --> 00:21:42.570
But, I can say this.

00:21:45.250 --> 00:21:47.320
We cannot run away.

00:22:29.310 --> 00:22:32.400
<b>I want to get to know you better,</b>

00:22:32.400 --> 00:22:35.490
<b>to go at each other with our true feelings.</b>

00:22:35.490 --> 00:22:41.830
<b>Your tears and smile are both here.</b>

00:22:42.290 --> 00:22:46.260
<b>No matter how hard it is, I won't be scared any more.</b>

00:22:46.260 --> 00:22:49.320
<b>With both of us, we can go anywhere.</b>

00:22:49.320 --> 00:22:54.760
<b>Since you're the one who taught me that I'm not alone.</b>

00:22:54.760 --> 00:23:02.450
<b>Every time I mutter the words "I was born to meet you"</b>

00:23:03.120 --> 00:23:07.490
<b>my unease disappears, and my heart burns stronger.</b>

00:23:07.880 --> 00:23:14.440
<b>Thank you. We'll go on together with a sign only we understand.</b>

00:23:14.880 --> 00:23:19.300
<b>Carve out this irreplaceable time!</b>

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:23.840
<b>I can't move away from here.</b>

00:23:23.840 --> 00:23:28.060
<b>Because I live feeling the same heartbeat.</b>

00:23:28.580 --> 00:23:30.280
<b>I want to protect you to the very last,</b>

00:23:30.280 --> 00:23:32.680
<b>to protect the promise built up.</b>

00:23:33.460 --> 00:23:40.080
<b>Thank you. We'll go on together with a sign only we understand.</b>

00:23:40.300 --> 00:23:45.810
<b>We are carving out this irreplaceable time!</b>

00:23:50.830 --> 00:23:52.620
On the next Heroman:

00:23:52.620 --> 00:23:53.070
The beach!

00:23:53.390 --> 00:23:55.010
And where there's a beach, there's sunlight!

00:23:55.010 --> 00:23:56.570
Where there's sunlight, there's summer!

00:23:56.570 --> 00:23:58.080
And when there's summer...

00:24:00.040 --> 00:24:05.330
Thanks to Hughes, Joey and the others were 
invited to a private government beach.

00:24:05.330 --> 00:24:07.040
Summer memories...

00:24:07.040 --> 00:24:09.380
A dazzling summer vacation...

00:24:09.380 --> 00:24:11.740
But what awaits them when they get there?

00:24:12.280 --> 00:24:15.980
Next time on Heroman #18: Separation.

00:24:15.980 --> 00:24:18.880
Heroman... Attack!
